WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.646
Today is the last six letters. They are made of slanting lines.

2
00:00:04.096 --> 00:00:10.909
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:12.513
These six letters.

4
00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:15.693
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

5
00:00:16.193 --> 00:00:19.156
Start at the dotted line. Slant down. Slant up.

6
00:00:20.883 --> 00:00:24.216
This one does it twice. Slant down, up, down, up.

7
00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:29.430
This one: slant down. Lift. Then slant back the other way.

8
00:00:30.981 --> 00:00:36.581
This one has a tail. A short slant down. Lift. Then a long slant, down below the line.

9
00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:41.321
This one: go across, slant back, and go across again.

10
00:00:42.993 --> 00:00:48.638
And this one is tall. Pull down from the top line. Lift. Then slant in, and slant out.

11
00:00:49.895 --> 00:00:55.928
Slanting letters are hard for small hands. Wobbly ones are fine. Where they start is what counts.

12
00:00:56.528 --> 00:00:59.540
Your child finger-traces all six, saying each path.

13
00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:03.669
Then press play on the listening track for job two, and step away.

14
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:08.737
The word is van.

15
00:01:09.637 --> 00:01:15.417
At the end, they write two letters and one word while you watch the pencil. That is every small letter done.
